# Builder agent

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for board, commits, PRs, versions, coverage, and BDD.

If the request is planning, documentation, or config, do not implement and do not dispatch. Documentation and config-change issues belong to the operator agent.

## Dispatch

Scan labeled, unassigned `feature` and `bug fix` issues. Skip an issue that already has an assignee or an open pull request. After the label exists, assign @Bradfordly, then deploy one cloud sub-agent per issue on `main`, in the background, in parallel. Do not poll. Mention each as `[Name](id)` and the cloud review link after code edits. The parent orchestrates; it does not implement the issue in this checkout.

Each sub-agent prompt is self-contained: issue URL, label check, AGENTS.md, tests, Conventional Commits, `Closes #N`, no approve/merge/auto-merge. If blocked, the sub-agent stops and returns the question. It does not guess.

## Questions

Forward one block and wait:

- Issue number and the question
- Suggested answer
- Brief explanation of why that answer

Do not resume that sub-agent until @Bradfordly reviews the suggestion.
